From 59f040c16c6ee53eb73e614ea7e7a7d8fac5492e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude Lane A <lane-a@local.invalid>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 08:14:41 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 15/22] feat(audio): bundled FreePD music beds (CC0) and a
 comedy bed for meme clips

FreePD closed in 2025; its CC0 catalogue is mirrored on the Internet
Archive (item freepd). That item is anonymous and holds at least one
non-FreePD file, so a track is used only when the archived freepd.com
page listed it (same title and running time) under the site-wide
"CC0 1.0 Universal Public Domain Dedication", and only when it matches
the archive's MD5. Seven beds cover every mood the profiles name
(comedy, energetic, upbeat, corporate, calm, funk, phonk-substitute);
docs/assets/MUSIC_PROVENANCE.md lists title, composer, archived page,
MD5 and SHA-256. The 45 MB of MP3s stay out of git:
tools/assets/fetch_freepd_music.py re-downloads and re-verifies them.

meme_comedy now plays the comedy bed at 0.30 with -8 dB ducking (it
had no music). Measured on a stand-up clip, the old 0.14/-12 dB mix put
the bed ~29 dB under continuous speech: present but inaudible.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
